WEBVTT

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.880
Who's that guy in the stripes?!

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.060
It seems he's not from JP's.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.140
Hibiki.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.470
Yamato's cell phone...

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.520
got a dead-face clip of me?

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.060
Yes.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.350
Going forward, the fight against
the Septentrion will intensify.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.780
You are a weapon.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.570
Nothing more.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.920
Did you think you could stop me?

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.960
Foolish.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:46.170
Yamato, you're so obstinate.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.000
I don't follow you.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.700
Good thing, huh Yamato?

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.300
What are you trying to say?

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:55.890
If you hadn't made it in time,
Hibiki would be dead.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.550
If nothing is done,
the dead-face clip is sure to come true.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:01.730
"Sure to"?

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.400
Drivel.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.140
The notion of set fate is ridiculous.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.740
Cause and effect can be
bent through strength.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.240
I see you haven't changed.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.520
"Strength"?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:15.030
What do YOU think?

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:17.030
What will you do?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:19.240
It's an important decision.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.200
Will you stay here?

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.510
Or will you go with Yamato?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.550
I...

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.040
I want to use this power for good.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:14.940
Hibiki! If you go back,
they'll just use you again!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.390
Ronaldo Kuruki, of the resistance
that would oppose Yamato.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.200
Is that right?

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:24.830
Right now, the decision lies with him.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.120
Would you mind please being quiet?

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:31.260
You seem to know what's going on, too.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.460
Can't you fill me in?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.140
You were told not to interfere, human.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.300
It spoke!

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.180
This is the demon that serves you?

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.850
Bifrons, you mustn't make any moves now.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.100
"Now"? What do you mean?

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.400
You'll see soon.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.890
Alcor.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:55.600
Why do you side with the humans?

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.240
I couldn't care what happens
to the puny creatures.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.230
Demon!

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.410
You all totally gutted
Nagoya, didn't you?!

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.490
You got the wrong idea, girl.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.290
You okay?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.620
Why you--!

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.750
Don't bother.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.960
You can't call your demons
right now, can you?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.720
You little runt!

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:19.090
"Runt"?

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.550
Now you've done it!

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.300
I'm gonna burn you for real!

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.820
No, Bifrons.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.140
I've said it twice now.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:28.270
I-I'm just kidding.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.140
That man isn't using a cell phone.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.100
Huh?

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:33.250
If he's not a Summoner,

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.650
standing there next to a demon is just strange.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.110
Are you a demon?

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.900
I see. That's what you think?

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.700
I get it.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.910
I am Alcor. The Anguished One.

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.690
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.290
"Anguished One"?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:54.020
Who am I?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.390
Even I'D like to know that.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:59.380
At the very least,
I don't intend to be your enemy.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.130
Don't skirt the issue.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.560
I wasn't trying to.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:10.270
I have yet to prepare an
answer that will satisfy you.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:13.310
Huh.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.560
You've assembled this many

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.500
humans able to use the summoning app?

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:27.950
We're taking you into custody.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:30.000
Don't try making a fuss, either.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:31.540
Bifrons.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.120
Gotcha.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.720
Bunch of pissants, ain't ya?

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.770
Stop it!

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.890
Ronaldo, have everyone fall back.

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.910
I'LL take him on.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.600
Oh, that's right.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:58.810
About your summoning app...

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:02.400
I was the one who gave it to you all.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.530
What was that?

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.650
Who are they?

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.780
They seem to be demons,

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.000
but there's no digital summoning signature.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:17.000
Sir... Is there something you still
haven't opened up to me about?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.210
What do you mean,
YOU gave us the summoning app?

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.630
You humans are weak.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:28.510
You'd be helpless before
a Septentrion attack.

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.220
That's pretty terrible, isn't it?

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:36.480
So I made the Nicaea site and
gave you these tools...

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:39.230
The choice to fight for life.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.530
He's the creator of the summoning app?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.570
That man... made the dead-face site?

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:51.030
Thanks to that, I was able to
find a new Sparkling One.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.970
Sparkling One...

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:55.830
No such concept exists.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.980
One is either gifted or incompetent.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.090
That is all that's needed
to understand humans.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:03.290
Will you take Hibiki back with you?

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:08.170
Hibiki. Will you stay here?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.850
Hibiki...

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:15.150
Septentrion will appear tomorrow.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:17.060
At the same time in three
different locations.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.850
According to the unbroken covenant.

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:24.390
Tokyo, Nagoya, Osaka.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.900
The next Septentrion will be Trinity,

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:30.480
a difficult type that will
attack three barriers at once.

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.700
That's right. Your trials
grow more difficult.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:38.060
Going forward, only Byakko-class
demons will be capable of fighting.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.590
Normal Summoners won't
have enough firepower.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.210
Just like the chief said, huh?

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:46.440
Hibiki. I entrust Osaka to you.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:47.840
Yamato!

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.510
And why not just say that at the start?

00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:51.650
Blabbermouth.

00:07:54.680 --> 00:07:55.560
Yamato.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:07:59.730
I... I don't intend to
be one of your pawns.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:04.400
Hibiki. What's this "correctness"
of which you speak?

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:10.290
I won't entrust my power
to others anymore.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.790
I will fight to protect
people of my own will.

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:16.200
I see. Irrelevant.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.570
The goal is eliminating the Septentrion.

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.840
That's all.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.210
On top of that...

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.120
I'll defeat all the enemies.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:30.010
And after that, if you try to make
some misguided future...

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.010
I'll stop you.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.140
You will stop me?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.020
Hibiki! Is that your choice?

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:42.560
It's something only I can do.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.390
Hibiki...

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:45.770
Interesting.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.930
If you can survive
till the end, that is.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.360
I'll survive.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.320
I look forward to it.

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.280
This day you defeat all the enemies.

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.250
Mr. former detective.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:03.410
You stay here and maintain command.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.130
Sir!

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:07.670
You're saying I should obey you?!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.310
That's right.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.460
Your careless actions have left the

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:15.530
Nagoya Branch with little
remaining firepower.

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:20.890
If you all don't fight tomorrow,
Nagoya will be destroyed.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:23.270
Ronaldo...

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:25.610
You have no choice.

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:27.780
We'll slay the enemy.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:31.570
But I won't let mankind's future
play out how you want!

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.150
Again, "If you can survive," that is.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:39.820
Survive...

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.370
Survive.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:46.370
We'll survive. For sure.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.290
Jeez, what the heck?!

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.790
So, that was JP's chief?

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.590
Yes. And who are you?

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.660
Airi Ban. And that's Jungo,
who was scouted with me.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.020
I'm Jungo.

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.470
Who's that guy in the stripes?

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:03.480
He's...

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.810
Huh? He's gone.

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:09.440
The Anguished One...

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:14.990
Yeah, but still...

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:19.490
Wasn't giving them the
demon-summoning app going too far?

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:23.250
I'm surprised by my own actions.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:27.470
I... What am I, I wonder?

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.460
Huh?

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.370
O Anguished One.

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.470
You won't overturn the Purge, will you?

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:37.340
I don't care what happens to the humans.

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:42.850
Perhaps I don't want to think the
humans are already a lost cause.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.850
You mean, the Sparkling One?

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.420
Yamato may have spurned me, but...

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.450
Over such a triviality.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.540
What are those clothes?

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:13.830
That's enough out of you.

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.510
I'm not coming back to this mansion.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:21.260
I see. How fast. You're
an adult now, eh?

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.220
It's begun.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:26.390
I will create the world of my ideals.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.970
"Might makes right," is that it?

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.810
Those with true abilities
should guide others.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.380
It will be a splendid world.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:36.400
So there's no other choice?

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:39.980
No. I shall bear humanity's fate.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:43.070
That's why I was born,
why I've lived thus far.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.540
The Purge of Polaris is without mercy.

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:50.540
Can you survive till
the final day, Yamato?

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.380
Of course I'll survive.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.430
I see. Well then, Yamato...

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:03.660
I certainly wish you'd
been the Sparkling One.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.540
Yamato came to rescue me?

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:19.110
Sparkling Ones... Friends...

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.600
It's all so complicated.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.300
Transport Terminal operation is stable.

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:48.840
Transport beginning in
5... 4... 3... 2... 1...

00:12:48.840 --> 00:12:50.060
Beginning transport!

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.060
Phase field is stable.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.820
Material composition of
biodata is in the clear.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:57.750
Magnetite consumption
is within normal levels.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:12:59.690
Transport is complete.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:08.750
Prof. Kanno.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.220
Please stop using yourself
for your transport tests.

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.190
"Tests"? It's functioning normally.

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.040
My adjustments are perfect.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:20.330
There's a more than 99%
chance I won't fail.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.050
Not 100%?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.090
In science, 100% is impossible.

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:27.640
I am neither God nor the devil.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:32.010
You finished adjusting the
transport Terminal yesterday

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:34.930
and the chief was delivered unharmed.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.730
Even without the Terminal,

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:39.240
the chief could have used his magic to fly there.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:41.940
But who knows if his
body could withstand it.

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.360
That's frightening.

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:44.070
Yes.

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:48.450
Failure, though improbable,
was a possibility.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.100
Is this Hibiki kid that important?

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:56.170
Sakocchi?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:14:00.590
Yes. At this point, Hibiki Kuze
has become an important...

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.000
weapon.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:06.300
Huh.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:07.830
Well, fine.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.520
Say, Fumi.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.440
What, Sakocchi?

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.160
Why do we have to do

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.350
physical checkups for all
staff at a time like this?

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:27.240
Ah. Don't worry about that.

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.870
They're just checking things out.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:35.580
Why a checkup all of a sudden?

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.000
Because even JP's is an organization?

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:38.880
What does that mean?

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.670
Like, managing the staff.

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:43.510
You have to do things by the rules
or you'll get in trouble, right?

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:45.790
But why at a time like this?

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.770
The government is just a façade.

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.220
The government, huh?

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:51.890
That adult stuff is such a pain.

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:53.680
Not that we'd know.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.430
Say, Hibiki...

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:59.020
Uh, no. It's nothing.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:05.520
Yesterday, if you and
Nitta hadn't come...

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.530
I would've been in trouble.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.700
Daichi, thank you.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.070
Idiot! No one's talkin' about that!

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.530
But if not for the two of you,

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.990
who knows what would've happened
when faced with Yamato.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:24.720
O-Oh. So it's a good
thing we came. I knew it!

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.890
You can count on me. We're friends!

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:30.560
There are four enemies to beat, right?

00:15:30.810 --> 00:15:32.310
Let's POW! get 'em!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:34.340
Yeah.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.440
How nice. He has close friends.

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:41.890
Yes. Hibiki and Shijima
are childhood friends.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:44.100
I meant you too, Io.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.020
If you two hadn't come yesterday,

00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:50.960
I'm sure Hibiki would have had a tough time.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.160
Okay, hold your breath.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:57.960
JP's is a strict organization.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:02.000
The truth is, people like you
all shouldn't be involved.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:05.170
Okay, fold your thumb
in and make a fist.

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:07.790
Why did you join JP's, Miss Otome?

00:16:07.790 --> 00:16:09.050
This needle will sting a bit.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:13.220
I was a doctor in Osaka. A normal one.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:13.970
Okay.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:17.470
One day, some people saying they
were from the government came.

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:20.230
They asked me, and I became
a doctor exclusively for JP's.

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:22.270
That kind of thing actually happens?

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:25.750
It looks like the government
knew I was well suited to

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.920
becoming a demonic Summoner.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.910
I had no idea myself, though.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.740
The government is scary, huh?

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:35.650
They know personal information

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:38.210
that even the person
in question doesn't.

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:42.650
Still, the pay is a heck
of a lot better here,

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:45.000
and my daughter is safe, thank goodness.

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.630
Huh? You have a daughter?!

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:50.470
This is her.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.180
She's very cute.

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.760
I'm a mysterious woman, aren't I?

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:59.160
Huh? No, I was just a little surprised.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:00.480
I respect you.

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:02.350
I've been respected.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:04.330
Being a mother is great!

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.690
She's not my real daughter, though.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.650
Okay, can you open up in front?

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.940
But being "real" or not doesn't matter.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:15.290
Because I love her.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.620
She drives me to keep going.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:20.250
Is that strange?

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:23.500
No, I think it's right.

00:17:24.660 --> 00:17:28.040
Thank you. I think you're right too, Io.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.400
Giving your all for your friends,
the person you like,

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.960
is definitely right.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.510
Yes...

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.270
Huh?! You said, someone I "like"?!

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:40.520
You're so cute, Io.

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:42.140
Hey!

00:17:46.480 --> 00:17:48.640
To do it at a time like THIS...

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:50.440
What do you think's going on?

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:53.940
What's this? What're you lookin' at?

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:55.190
Joe!

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.650
That's bad, ain't it?

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:58.660
But I get it.

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.320
Io is pretty all right.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:03.370
What are you talking about Nitta for?

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.790
So I'm right, young man.

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.460
Well, if it was me,

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.460
I'd act like I'd made a mistake,
throw open the door and--

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.430
Joe!

00:18:14.430 --> 00:18:15.920
What is it, Daichi?

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:19.700
Hibiki! It's nothin'!

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.140
Hibiki, this here is a
scientific investigation.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:33.490
H-Hibiki?!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:37.390
Oh. Uh, no, I didn't!

00:18:37.390 --> 00:18:39.870
That's right. This is Joe's fault!

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:42.950
He took off!

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:45.500
Being a peeping tom is...

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.040
The worst!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.500
That was terrible, Daichi.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:51.560
She'll want nothing to do with us.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.130
It's a misunderstanding!

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:56.140
I never thought Nitta was really there.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:58.760
How nice. The bloom of youth.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.290
Joe, you took off too fast!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:04.350
I said, that's how it gets
when you're me, didn't I?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:05.360
You all.

00:19:06.970 --> 00:19:08.190
Hey, Kurikki.

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:09.520
Kuri...?

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.600
Ronaldo, you're doing
an examination, too?

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:16.290
That's right. If I have
my comrades do it,

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:18.540
I can't very well not do it myself.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:19.530
Huh.

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.160
You didn't have any doubts?

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:25.290
I thoroughly examined the medicine
and equipment ahead of time.

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:26.990
Oh, jeez.

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.880
Also...

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:29.780
This may be an unprecedented

00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.440
time in human history, but
that doesn't change things.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.220
We can't have our bodies falling ill.

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:37.750
You've thought things through that far?

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:39.220
I have now.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.510
See you.

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.850
I really don't care for that guy.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:50.770
Really?

00:19:51.680 --> 00:19:53.980
Kurikki's trying his hardest.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:54.860
Everyone is.

00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.620
YOU don't seem to be, Joe.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.490
Daichi, that stings!

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.490
Ah! There you are, you dirty peepers!

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:04.740
You sick perverts!

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.080
We weren't peeping or anything.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.460
You're making excuses?!

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:08.990
Call them excuses if you like,

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:11.000
but it's not like you knew where we were!

00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:13.420
How could I NOT know?!

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:21.420
Idiot! Pervert! Molester!

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:22.740
You have the wrong idea!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:24.910
There's nothing wrong about it!

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.210
How should I go about
erasing your memories?!

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.930
H-H-Hey!

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.350
Oh, speaking of...

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.650
You have a cute bellybutton.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:36.020
You spied on her?

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.270
It was an accident.

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:37.860
I see.

00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:39.820
Don't accept this!

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:46.130
It seems there was some trouble
at the Nagoya Branch.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:47.370
Is everything all right?

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:49.080
Yes. Not to worry.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:54.210
Yamato, it seems you left here
yesterday, didn't you?

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:58.210
You must protect Tokyo,
isn't that right?

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:02.670
Is that not what the
Hotsuin, what JP's is for?

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:05.040
We cannot have anything happen to us.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:09.230
That would set a bad example
to our constituents.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.470
Worthless garbage.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:17.740
Simultaneous manifestation readings
in Tokyo, Osaka, and Nagoya!

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:19.860
They're all in the ocean.

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:21.770
The readings are still faint.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:23.610
The ocean, huh?

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:26.200
At this rate, a land
attack will be no use.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.820
The plan was in consideration of the

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.470
maximum casualty limit for the cities,

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:33.750
with the water stopping the
Septentrion from coming on land.

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:35.960
Hurry and plot their landing point.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:36.550
Ma'am!

00:21:37.040 --> 00:21:39.190
Also, evacuate the civilians from

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.930
the Septentrion's projected
route, just in case.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:44.630
Evacuate? For what reason?

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:48.310
Irrelevant. Command of
this plan rests with me.

00:21:48.310 --> 00:21:50.190
You're losing your cool.

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:51.560
Think you can do this?

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:57.110
Destroying the enemy
takes precedence. Right?

00:21:57.560 --> 00:21:59.750
Got an incoming from Tokyo. Here goes.

00:22:01.060 --> 00:22:02.990
Whoa, she's a hottie!

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:04.360
Makoto Sako.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:06.530
It's been a while, Ronaldo Kuriki.

00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:09.280
He knows her?

00:22:09.610 --> 00:22:11.120
Looks like something happened
between 'em, huh?

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:13.710
I'll explain the plan's outline.

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:17.580
The three Megrez are connected
as one via phase space.

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:19.210
Unless we stop all
three of them at once,

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:21.370
any damage rendered will be useless.

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:22.840
A simultaneous attack, huh?

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:26.760
Most of you at Nagoya
Branch are civilians,

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:29.600
but you have more firepower
than a normal JP's squad.

00:22:30.260 --> 00:22:32.930
We must win, no matter what.

00:22:33.550 --> 00:22:34.100
Please.

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:36.100
You don't have to tell us twice.

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:38.480
We WILL defeat the enemy.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:43.450
Hibiki Kuze. You all will protect Osaka.

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:47.110
What is this? It's scary!

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:48.700
Makoto.

00:22:49.320 --> 00:22:51.930
We're no longer members of JP's.

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:53.210
I know that.

00:22:53.910 --> 00:22:56.670
We place our hopes in you as our friend.

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:57.910
Very well.

00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:03.340
Huh? Speaking of, who's handling Tokyo?

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:10.890
I alone will be plenty.

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:21.690
Hibiki.

00:23:23.910 --> 00:23:25.200
Hinako!

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:26.650
You'll all right?!

00:23:27.110 --> 00:23:29.570
Who said I was dead?

00:23:31.530 --> 00:23:33.040
Thank goodness!

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:38.160
I thought... both you and Keita...

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:42.880
Welcome back. You've been through a lot.

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:55.930
Fumi. What are you doing.
You're supposed to be on standby.

00:23:56.390 --> 00:23:57.630
I've found it.

00:23:58.060 --> 00:23:58.900
Found what?

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:02.400
The sacrifice to present to Lugh.

00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:03.820
What?

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:08.610
Sacrifice?
